{′} & =2{x}_{3}^{2}-2{y}_{3} \\\\  & =2\\cdot {1}^{2}-2\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,{y}_{1}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,{y}_{2}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,{y}_{3}^{′}\\,$ | $Δy$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $-2$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $-2$ | $4$ |  |\n\nFinally, we compute $Δy$ using the Runge-Kutta Method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & =\\frac{1}{6}({y}^{′}+2{y}_{1}^{′}+2{y}_{2}^{′}+{y}_{3}^{′})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}(-2+2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}+2\\cdot (-2)+4)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the completed first row is as given below.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,{y}_{1}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,{y}_{2}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,{y}_{3}^{′}\\,$ | $Δy$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $-2$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $-2$ | $4$ | $-\\frac{1}{6}$ |\n\nTo get the values of $x$ and $y$ in the *next* row, we add $Δx$ to $x$ and $Δy$ to $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{\\text{new}} & =x+Δx \\\\  & =0+1 \\\\  & =1 \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\  & =1+(-\\frac{1}{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding these rows to our table gives the following:\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,{y}_{1}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,{y}_{2}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,{y}_{3}^{′}\\,$ | $Δy$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $-2$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $-2$ | $4$ | $-\\frac{1}{6}$ |\n| $1$ | $\\frac{5}{6}$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(1)≈\\frac{5}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534849 true] [17592186314665 1000 #edb/ref 17592186314666 13194139534849 true] [17592186314665 1000 #edb/ref 17592186314667 13194139534849 true] [17592186314665 1000 #edb/ref 17592186314668 13194139534849 true] [17592186314665 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045451 13194139534849 true] [17592186314665 1041 "field-1" 13194139534849 true] [17592186314665 1104 #edb/ref 1759